ticks"],"zh":["AI代理任务管理","Ticks设置指南","AI工具任务管理","持续循环运行","Web监控","CLI命令行管理","任务依赖管理","持久历史和笔记"],"ja":["AIエージェントのタスク管理","Ticksセットアップガイド","AIツールのタスク管理","継続的なループ実行","Web監視","CLIコマンドライン管理","タスク依存管理","持続的な履歴とノート"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 작업 관리","Ticks 설정 가이드","AI 도구 작업 관리","연속 루프 실행","웹 모니터링","CLI 명령줄 관리","작업 의존성 관리","지속적인 기록과 노트"],"es":["agentes de inteligencia artificial","herramientas de seguimiento de problemas","línea de comandos tk","gestión de tareas","seguimiento de agentes","tablero web","dependencias entre tareas","historial persistente"],"fr":["agents d''intelligence artificielle","outils de suivi de problèmes","ligne de commande tk","gestion de tâches","suivi des agents","tableau de bord web","dépendances entre tâches","historique persistant"],"de":["künstliche Intelligenz-Agenten","Werkzeuge zur Fehlerverfolgung","Kommandozeile tk","Aufgabenverwaltung","Verfolgung von Agenten","web-basiertes Dashboard","Abhängigkeiten zwischen Aufgaben","persistente Historie"],"pt":["rastreador de problemas para IA","ferramentas de IA","CLI para gerenciamento de tarefas","execução contínua de agentes","quadro web para monitoramento","dependências entre tarefas","histórico persistente"],"ru":["отслеживатель проблем для ИИ","ИИ инструменты","CLI для управления задачами","непрерывное выполнение агентов","веб-доска для мониторинга","зависимости между задачами","постоянная история"],"ar":["عامل تتبع للمشاكل لأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","واجهة سطر الأوامر لإدارة المهام","تنفيذ متواصل للوكلاء","لوحة ويب للرصد","اعتماد بين المهام","سجل دائم"]}},"owner":"pengelbrecht","repo":"ticks","repoPath":"pengelbrecht/ticks","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.549Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ticks","description":"Work with Ticks issue tracker and AI agent runner. Use when managing tasks or issues with tk commands, running AI agents on epics, creating ticks from a SPEC.md, or working in a repo with a .tick directory. Triggers on phrases like create ticks, tk, run ticker, epic, close the task, plan this, break this down.","bodyPreview":"# Ticks Workflow\n\nTicks is an issue tracker designed for AI agents. The `tk` CLI manages tasks, runs agents in continuous loops, and provides a web-based board for monitoring.\n\n## When to Use Ticks vs TodoWrite\n\n**Use Ticks (`tk`) for work that:**\n- Spans multiple sessions or conversations\n- Has dependencies on other tasks\n- Is discovered during other work and should be tracked\n- Needs human handoff or approval gates\n- Benefits from persistent history and notes\n\n**Use TodoWrite for:**\n- Simple s","body":"# Ticks Workflow\n\nTicks is an issue tracker designed for AI agents. The `tk` CLI manages tasks, runs agents in continuous loops, and provides a web-based board for monitoring.\n\n## When to Use Ticks vs TodoWrite\n\n**Use Ticks (`tk`) for work that:**\n- Spans multiple sessions or conversations\n- Has dependencies on other tasks\n- Is discovered during other work and should be tracked\n- Needs human handoff or approval gates\n- Benefits from persistent history and notes\n\n**Use TodoWrite for:**\n- Simple single-session tasks\n- Work that will be completed in the current conversation\n- Tracking progress on immediate work\n\nDon''t over-index on creating ticks for every small thing. Use your judgment.\n\n## Skill Workflow\n\nWhen invoked, follow this workflow:\n\n### Step 0: Check Prerequisites\n\n**1. Git repository:**\n```bash\ngit status 2>/dev/null || git init\n```\n\n**2. Ticks initialized:**\n```bash\nls .tick/ 2>/dev/null || tk init\n```\n\n**3. tk installed:**\n```bash\nwhich tk || echo \"Install: curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengelbrecht/ticks/main/scripts/install.sh | sh\"\n```\n\n**4. Git tracking (important):**\n\nThe `.tick/` directory should be tracked by git, not gitignored. Ticks are designed to be version-controlled so they sync across machines and team members via normal git workflows.\n\nIf you see `.tick` or `.tick/` in the project''s `.gitignore`, remove it. The only things that should be gitignored are internal/local files, which is handled by `.tick/.gitignore` (ignores `.index.json` and `logs/`).\n\n```bash\n# Check if .tick is gitignored (should return nothing)\ngit check-ignore .tick/\n\n# If it returns \".tick/\", remove the entry from .gitignore\n```\n\n### Step 1: Check for SPEC.md\n\nLook for a SPEC.md (or similar spec file) in the repo root.\n\n**If no spec exists:** Go to Step 2a (Create Spec)\n**If spec exists but incomplete:** Go to Step 2b (Complete Spec)\n**If spec is complete:** Skip to Step 3 (Create Ticks)\n\n### Step 2a: Create Spec Through Conversation\n\nHave a natural conversation with the user to understand their idea:\n\n1. **Let them describe it** - Don''t interrupt, let them explain the full vision\n2. **Ask clarifying questions** - Dig into unclear areas through back-and-forth dialogue\n3. **Optionally use AskUserQuestion** - For quick multiple-choice decisions\n4. **Write SPEC.md** - Once you have enough detail, generate the spec\n\n**Conversation topics to explore:**\n- What problem does this solve? Who''s it for?\n- Core features vs nice-to-haves\n- Technical constraints or preferences\n- How will users interact with it?\n- What does \"done\" look like?\n\n### Step 2b: Complete Existing Spec\n\nIf SPEC.md exists but has gaps:\n\n1. **Read the spec** - Identify what''s missing or unclear\n2. **Ask targeted questions** - Focus on the gaps, don''t re-ask obvious things\n3. **Update SPEC.md** - Fill in the missing details\n\n## Creating Good Tasks\n\n**Every task should be an atomic, committable piece of work with tests.**\n\nThe ideal task:\n- Has a clear, single deliverable\n- Can be verified by running tests\n- Results in demoable software that builds on previous work\n- Is completable in 1-3 agent iterations\n\n**Good task:**\n```bash\ntk create \"Add email validation to registration\" \\\n  -d \"Validate email format on blur, show error below input.\n\nTest cases:\n- valid@example.com -> valid\n- invalid@ -> invalid\n- @nodomain.com -> invalid\n\nRun: go test ./internal/validation/...\" \\\n  -acceptance \"All validation tests pass\" \\\n  -parent <epic-id>\n```\n\n**Bad task:**\n```bash\ntk create \"Add email validation\" -d \"Make sure emails are valid\"\n# No test cases, no verification criteria - agent will guess\n```\n\nSee `references/tick-patterns.md` for more patterns.\n\n### Step 3: Create Ticks from Spec\n\nTransform the spec into ticks organized by epic.\n\n**For phased specs:** Focus on creating ticks for the current/next phase only. Don''t create ticks for future phases - they may change based on learnings.\n\n**Epic organization:**\n1. Group related tasks into logical epics (auth, API, UI, etc.)\n2. Create tasks with dependencies using `-blocked-by`\n3. Mark human-required tasks with `--awaiting work`\n\n**Designing for parallel execution:**\nTasks in the same wave (no blocking relationship) may run concurrently. To avoid file conflicts:\n- If two tasks edit the same file, make one block the other\n- Use `tk graph <epic>` to visualize waves and verify parallel tasks touch different files\n- Example: Task A edits `auth.go`, Task B edits `auth.go` → B should block on A\n\n```bash\n# Create epics\ntk create \"Authentication\" -t epic\ntk create \"API Endpoints\" -t epic\n\n# Create tasks with acceptance criteria\ntk create \"Add JWT token generation\" \\\n  -d \"Implement JWT signing and verification\" \\\n  -acceptance \"JWT tests pass\" \\\n  -parent <auth-epic>\n\ntk create \"Add login endpoint\" \\\n  -d \"POST /api/login with email/password\" \\\n  -acceptance \"Login endpoint tests pass\" \\\n  -parent <api-epic> \\\n  -blocked-by <jwt-task>\n\n# Human-only tasks (skipped by tk next)\ntk create \"Set up production database\" --awaiting work \\\n  -d \"Create RDS instance and configure access\"\n\ntk create \"Create Stripe API keys\" --awaiting work \\\n  -d \"Set up Stripe account and get API credentials\"\n```\n\n### Step 4: Guide User Through Blocking Human Tasks\n\nIf human tasks block automated tasks, guide the user through them before running the agent.\n\n```bash\n# Check for blocking human tasks\ntk list --awaiting work\ntk blocked  # See what''s waiting\n```\n\nWalk the user through each blocking task, then close it:\n```bash\ntk close <id> \"Completed - connection string in .env\"\n```\n\n### Step 5: Choose Execution Mode\n\nTicks supports two execution approaches. If the user hasn''t specified a preference, ask:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"How would you like to execute this epic?\"\nHeader: \"Execution\"\nOptions:\n  - \"tk run\" - \"Rich monitoring via tickboard, HITL support, cost tracking, git worktree isolation\"\n  - \"Claude Code\" - \"Native parallel subagents, seamless session execution, direct visibility\"\n```\n\n#### Option A: tk run\n\nUses the Ticks agent runner with tickboard monitoring.\n\n```bash\n# Run on specific epic\ntk run <epic-id>\n\n# Pool mode - N concurrent workers within single epic\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4\n\n# Pool with custom stale timeout\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4 --stale-timeout 2h\n\n# Run in isolated worktree\ntk run <epic-id> --worktree\n\n# Parallel epics (each in own worktree)\ntk run <epic-id> --parallel 2\n\n# Combined: parallel epics with pool workers each\ntk run epic1 epic2 --parallel 2 --pool 4\n\n# With cost limit\ntk run <epic-id> --max-cost 5.00\n```\n\n**Monitor:** `tk board` opens local web interface.\n\n**Best for:** Production epics, rich HITL workflows, long-running tasks, cost tracking.\n\n#### Option B: Claude Code Native\n\nUses Claude Code''s Task tool to spawn parallel subagents.\n\n**Best for:** Quick parallel execution within a Claude session, direct visibility into agents.\n\nSee **`references/claude-runner.md`** for full documentation including:\n- Task tool parameters and options\n- Agent naming conventions (epic/tick/wave)\n- Wave orchestration algorithm\n- Polling strategy to avoid hangs\n- HITL-aware state transitions\n- Example session\n\n#### Quick Comparison\n\n| Aspect | `tk run` | Claude Code |\n|--------|----------|-------------|\n| Monitoring | Tickboard | Claude Code UI |\n| HITL | Rich (approvals, checkpoints) | Basic (conversation) |\n| Parallelization | Pool workers (`--pool`) or worktrees (`--parallel`) | Task subagents |\n| File isolation | Worktrees (proven) | Shared workspace |\n| State persistence | Tick files (survives crashes) | Session-bound |\n| Cost tracking | Built-in (`--max-cost`) | Manual |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Creating Ticks\n\n```bash\ntk create \"Title\" -d \"Description\" -acceptance \"Tests pass\"  # Task\ntk create \"Title\" -t epic                                    # Epic\ntk create \"Title\" -parent <epic-id>                          # Under epic\ntk create \"Title\" -blocked-by <task-id>                      # Blocked\ntk create \"Title\" --awaiting work                            # Human task\ntk create \"Title\" --requires approval                        # Needs approval gate\n```\n\n### Querying\n\n```bash\ntk list                      # All open ticks\ntk list -t epic              # Epics only\ntk list -parent <epic-id>    # Tasks in epic\ntk ready                     # Unblocked tasks\ntk next <epic-id>            # Next task for agent\ntk blocked                   # Blocked tasks\ntk list --awaiting           # Tasks awaiting human\ntk graph <epic-id>           # Dependency graph with parallelization\ntk graph <epic-id> --json    # JSON output for agents\n```\n\n### Managing\n\n```bash\ntk show <id>                 # Show details\ntk close <id> \"reason\"       # Close tick\ntk note <id> \"text\"          # Add note\ntk approve <id>              # Approve awaiting tick\ntk reject <id> \"feedback\"    # Reject with feedback\n```\n\n### Running Agent (Two Modes)\n\n**Mode A: Native tk run**\n```bash\ntk run <epic-id>                      # Run on epic\ntk run --auto                         # Auto-select epic\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4             # Pool mode (4 concurrent workers)\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4 --stale-timeout 2h  # Custom stale timeout\ntk run <epic-id> --worktree           # Use git worktree\ntk run <epic-id> --parallel 3         # 3 epics in parallel worktrees\ntk run a b --parallel 2 --pool 4      # 2 epics, 4 workers each\ntk run <epic-id> --max-iterations 10  # Limit iterations\ntk run <epic-id> --max-cost 5.00      # Cost limit\ntk run <epic-id> --watch              # Restart when tasks ready\ntk board                              # Web interface\n```\n\n**Mode B: Claude Code Native**\n```bash\n# See references/claude-runner.md for full details\n\n# 1. Get dependency graph\ntk graph <epic-id> --json\n\n# 2. Ask user for MAX_AGENTS (1-10)\n\n# 3. For each wave, launch Task agents:\n#    Task(subagent_type: \"general-purpose\",\n#         name: \"<epic>-w<wave>-<tick>\",\n#         run_in_background: true,\n#         mode: \"bypassPermissions\")\n\n# 4. Poll for completion, sync to ticks\ntk close <tick-id> --reason \"Completed via Claude runner\"\n```\n\n### Planning Parallel Execution\n\nBefore running agents, use `tk graph` to understand parallelization opportunities:\n\n```bash\ntk graph <epic-id>        # Human-readable wave breakdown\ntk graph <epic-id> --json # Machine-readable for planning\n```\n\nThe graph shows:\n- **Waves**: Groups of tasks that can run in parallel\n- **Max parallel**: How many workers you could use at once\n- **Critical path**: Minimum sequential steps to complete the epic\n- **Dependencies**: What each task is blocked by\n\nUse this to decide:\n- `--pool N` for N concurrent workers within one epic (recommended)\n- `--parallel N` for N epics in separate worktrees\n- Combine both: `--parallel 2 --pool 4` for 2 epics with 4 workers each\n\nSee `references/tk-commands.md` for full reference.\n\n## Assisting with Awaiting Ticks\n\nWhen working interactively, help users process awaiting ticks:\n\n```bash\ntk list --awaiting    # Find ticks awaiting human\ntk next --awaiting    # Next one needing attention\n```\n\nUse AskUserQuestion to help users decide, then execute:\n\n```bash\n# User approves\ntk approve <id>\n\n# User rejects\ntk reject <id> \"feedback here\"\n\n# User provides input\ntk note <id> \"Use sliding window algorithm\" --from human\ntk approve <id>\n```\n\nAlways use `--from human` when adding notes on behalf of the user.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:11:23.697Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code needing task management and issue tracking capabilities across multiple sessions","zh":"适合于像Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code这样的AI代理，需要跨多个会话进行任务管理和问题跟踪的能力","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、Claude CodeなどのAIエージェントに適しており、複数のセッションをまたいでのタスク管理と問題追跡の機能が必要","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 여러 세션에 걸쳐 작업 관리 및 문제 추적 기능이 필요","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que necesitan capacidades de gestión de tareas y seguimiento de problemas en varias sesiones","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code nécessitant des capacités de gestion de tâches et de suivi de problèmes sur plusieurs sessions","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die Aufgabenmanagement- und Problemmelderfunktionen über mehrere Sitzungen hinweg benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que necessitam de capacidades de gerenciamento de tarefas e acompanhamento de problemas em várias sessões","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, которым необходимы возможности управления задачами и отслеживания проблем на протяжении нескольких сессий","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكيين مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات إدارة المهام وتتبع المشكلات عبر عدة جلسات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage tasks with dependencies, track issues discovered during work, and utilize a web-based board for monitoring, all while leveraging the `tk` CLI for continuous agent loops and human handoff or approval gates","zh":"赋予代理管理具有依赖关系的任务、跟踪工作过程中发现的问题、并利用基于Web的看板进行监控的能力，同时利用`tk` CLI进行持续的代理循环和人工交接或批准门","ja":"エージェントが依存関係のあるタスクを管理し、作業中に発見された問題を追跡し、Webベースのボードを使用してリアルタイムで監視およびコラボレーションを行い、`tk` CLIを使用して継続的なエージェントループと人間によるハンドオーバーまたは承認ゲートを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 종속성 있는 작업을 관리하고, 작업 중에 발견 된 문제를 추적하고, 웹 기반 보드를 사용하여 실시간 모니터링 및 협력을 수행하며, `tk` CLI를 사용하여 연속 에이전트 루프 및 인간의 인수 또는 승인 게이트를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar tareas con dependencias, rastrear problemas descubiertos durante el trabajo y utilizar una pizarra web para el monitoreo, todo mientras aprovecha el `tk` CLI para bucles de agentes continuos y puertas de entrega o aprobación humanas","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des tâches avec des dépendances, de suivre les problèmes découverts au cours du travail et d''utiliser un tableau Web pour la surveillance, le tout en exploitant le `tk` CLI pour des boucles d''agents continues et des portes de remise ou d''approbation humaines","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Aufgaben mit Abhängigkeiten zu verwalten, Probleme zu verfolgen, die während der Arbeit entdeckt werden, und eine Web-Tafel für die Überwachung zu nutzen, während sie den `tk` CLI für kontinuierliche Agentenschleifen und menschliche Übergabe- oder Genehmigungsschranken nutzen","pt":"Permite que os agentes gerenciem tarefas com dependências, rastreiem problemas descobertos durante o trabalho e utilizem uma placa baseada na web para monitoramento, tudo isso aproveitando o `tk` CLI para loops de agente contínuos e portões de aprovação ou entrega manual","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять задачами с зависимостями, отслеживать проблемы, обнаруженные во время работы, и использовать веб-ориентированную доску для мониторинга, все это при помощи `tk` CLI для непрерывных циклов агента и ворот ручной передачи или утверждения","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء إدارة المهام مع التبعيات، وتتبع المشكلات التي تم اكتشافها أثناء العمل، واستخدام لوحة قائمة على الويب للرصد، كل ذلك بالاستفادة من `tk` CLI للدوائر المستمرة للوكيل وأبواب الموافقة أو التسليم اليدوي"},"useCases":{"en":["Managing complex projects with multiple dependencies","Tracking issues across sessions and conversations","Utilizing a web-based board for real-time monitoring and collaboration"],"zh":["管理具有多个依赖关系的复杂项目","跨会话和对话跟踪问题","利用基于Web的看板进行实时监控和协作"],"ja":["複数の依存関係を持つ複雑なプロジェクトの管理","セッションや会話をまたいでの問題の追跡","Webベースのボードを使用したリアルタイムの監視とコラボレーション"],"ko":["여러 종속성을 가진 복잡한 프로젝트 관리","세션 및 대화 전반에 걸친 문제 추적","웹 기반 보드를 사용한 실시간 모니터링 및 협력"],"es":["Gestión de proyectos complejos con múltiples dependencias","Seguimiento de problemas en varias sesiones y conversaciones","Uso de una pizarra web para la monitorización y la colaboración en tiempo real"],"fr":["Gestion de projets complexes avec plusieurs dépendances","Suivi de problèmes sur plusieurs sessions et conversations","Utilisation d''un tableau Web pour la surveillance et la collaboration en temps réel"],"de":["Verwaltung komplexer Projekte mit mehreren Abhängigkeiten","Verfolgung von Problemen über mehrere Sitzungen und Gespräche hinweg","Nutzung einer Web-Tafel für die Echtzeitüberwachung und -zusammenarbeit"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de projetos complexos com várias dependências","Rastreamento de problemas em várias sessões e conversas","Utilização de uma placa baseada na web para monitoramento e colaboração em tempo real"],"ru":["Управление сложными проектами с множеством зависимостей","Отслеживание проблем на протяжении нескольких сессий и разговоров","Использование веб-ориентированной доски для мониторинга и сотрудничества в реальном времени"],"ar":["إدارة مشاريع معقدة مع عدة تبعيات","تتبع المشكلات عبر عدة جلسات ومحادثات","استخدام لوحة قائمة على الويب للرصد والتعاون في الوقت الفعلي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires `tk` CLI for task management","Designed specifically for AI agents and teams working on complex projects"],"zh":["需要`tk` CLI进行任务管理","专门为AI代理和处理复杂项目的团队设计"],"ja":["タスク管理には`tk` CLIが必要","複雑なプロジェクトを扱うAIエージェントやチーム向けに特に設計"],"ko":["작업 관리를 위해 `tk` CLI가 필요","복잡한 프로젝트를 처리하는 AI 에이전트 및 팀을 위해 특별히 설계"],"es":["Requiere `tk` CLI para la gestión de tareas","Diseñado específicamente para agentes de IA y equipos que trabajan en proyectos complejos"],"fr":["Nécessite `tk` CLI pour la gestion des tâches","Conçu spécifiquement pour les agents IA et les équipes travaillant sur des projets complexes"],"de":["Benötigt `tk` CLI für die Aufgabenverwaltung","Speziell für KI-Agents und Teams entwickelt, die an komplexen Projekten arbeiten"],"pt":["Exige `tk` CLI para gerenciamento de tarefas","Projetado especificamente para agentes de IA e equipes que trabalham em projetos complexos"],"ru":["Требует `tk` CLI для управления задачами","Разработан специально для агентов ИИ и команд, работающих над сложными проектами"],"ar":["يتطلب `tk` CLI لإدارة المهام","صمم خصيصًا للوكلاء الذكيين والفرق التي تعمل على مشاريع معقدة"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"48c92cd081e421ff13b083947511f42c09fa222eae38a988f4b1d4d233df9f38","qualityScore":60}');
